# Public API, ownership and parity proof

## Owning resource coverage

| Original storage | Additive owning surface | Payload seen by lower engine |
|---|---|---|
| BoundsSet shapes | JobRasterScratch.bounds | ShapeBounds slice |
| BoundaryMask bits | boundary_bits, Boundary pool | u8 slice, original bit addressing |
| ScanlineIndex events/nodes/roots/shape events/nodes | scanline_events/scanline_nodes/scanline_roots/shape_events/shape_nodes | original ScanlineEvent/ScanlineNode/i32/ShapeRowEvent |
| RowBuffers offsets/active edges/shapes | shape_offsets/active_edges/active_shapes | usize/u32 slices |
| FillCache eligibility/crossings/intervals/runs | eligible_shapes/crossings/intervals/pixel_runs | bool/FillCrossing/FillInterval/PixelRun slices |
| Local edges/seams | local_edges/dash_seams | Edge/bool slices |
| DashCache segments/joins/shapes | JobDashCache with typed buffers | original DashSegment/DashJoin plus allocation-free JobDashRange |
| Nested per-shape grids | JobDashRange.grid_cells/grid_refs | JobDashView.grid resolves original GridCell/u32 slices |
| Cached center/subpixel/stroke cost | center_samples/subpixel_samples/stroke_cost | u8/usize slices |
| Root/child scratch | multiple JobRasterScratch descriptors | all allocated by the SAME RasterJob/ChargeLedger |
| Group scratch | GroupScratch pool | typed u8 buffer, 64 MiB aggregate |
| Packed output | Output pool/JobRenderOutput | checked u8 slice, no unleased Tile transfer |

Engine-only scalar counts/cursors/flags, scanline AVL state, five interval counts,
stride, fill-row work, view mapping and shape ranges remain allocation-free state.
The API changes storage access, not the corresponding algorithms. `JobElement`
is sealed and Copy-only; nested heap storage cannot hide inside an element.

## Reservation and publication

The coordinator constructs one ChargeLedger with its canonical source owner and
explicit job budget, then transfers it into RasterJob. Existing external active
leases are rejected; JobStartError returns the original ledger unchanged. Job
handles bind ledger identity, slot and monotonic insertion serial and never expose
a lease or Vec. Empty live buffers retain a zero-byte registry lease. The source
Arc is retained once by the ledger and charged by actual capacity once.

Slot registry replacement is itself admitted through an active ledger lease.
ChargeLedger's own entry registry uses the existing checked old/new reserve
implementation. Payload allocation mints an entry, verifies requested arithmetic,
local caps, total budget, history and count, then reserves requested bytes in
that active entry BEFORE calling real Vec::try_reserve_exact. Old buffers remain
charged throughout. Exclusive ledger access holds remaining available capacity
until actual capacity is known. Actual capacity is checked against the per-buffer
cap, local aggregate caps and same global budget before any publication. Native
allocator excess can only be observed after return; rejected excess is dropped.
This is Vec-capacity admission, not allocator/RSS measurement or an absolute
allocator transient-size guarantee.

Growth/shrink/append stage original Copy records plus the new suffix in admitted
storage, polling SourceRead per copy and checking control at publication. Errors
preserve old contents/capacity/token/lease. Successful physical reserves remain
in history even if subsequent copy/control fails. Metadata capacity can remain
after a failed operation, honestly reflected in stats. In-capacity append rolls
back just its unpublished suffix. No whole source/cache clone, hidden Vec clone,
infallible Drop allocation, unsafe block or added dependency is used.

## Lifecycle/error coverage

| Operation/error | Proof |
|---|---|
| source once, Send job, Drop cleanup | source_once_owned_drop_and_no_self_reference; weak owner expires while token copy survives |
| actual spare capacity/history/reuse | actual_spare_capacity_reuse_growth_clear_release_history |
| grow requires old+new overlap before allocation | overlap_rejected_before_alloc_and_old_buffer_unchanged |
| native reserve failure | real_try_reserve_failure_and_checked_byte_overflow_preserve_state uses actual try_reserve_exact above isize::MAX; no global OOM claim |
| arithmetic/token/history/count overflow | new byte-overflow integration plus two private boundary-state unit proofs |
| registry pressure / registration rollback | metadata_pressure_leaves_no_published_buffers_or_external_lease_escape; scratch_registration_failure_rolls_back_tokens_not_physical_history |
| wrong source/job/stale/double | stale_double_wrong_job_and_equal_bytes_wrong_source_rejected; empty-source Arc identity proof |
| cancellation after actual allocation / during old copy / suffix | cancel_before_publication_retains_real_allocation_history_not_contents; growth_copy_loop_cancellation_and_in_capacity_append_are_atomic; cancellation_inside_append_preserves_old_capacity_and_contents |
| nested actual capacity/global grid caps/reuse | nested_grids_share_source_budget_actual_capacity_and_stale_checks; global_grid_capacity_limits_admit_before_allocation_and_release_for_reuse |
| physical shrink/clear/release | physical_shrink_reserves_overlap_and_preserves_history_and_values |
| wrong pool/duplicate/mismatched descriptor | wrong_pool_output_dash_and_grid_are_rejected; duplicate_or_wrong_scratch_descriptor_cannot_partially_release; output_layout_caps_and_wrong_scratch_roles_are_rejected |
| discarded descriptor cleanup | release_all_reclaims_discarded_descriptors_and_invalidates_saved_tokens |
| same-job real index row writes + child/output | actual_lower_index_sample_and_child_output_share_one_job |

`truncate` retains capacity; `clear_capacity` keeps the same empty live token;
`release` invalidates token copies. Descriptor Drop is NOT resource release.
Scratch release prevalidates uniqueness/roles/liveness without work control,
then releases its fixed buffers. Nested grids are independently job-owned and
may be shared; release them explicitly or use release_all/finish/Drop. release_all
reclaims every payload even after all descriptor copies are discarded. finish
also destroys both registries and ends this job's source charge, returning zero
job-live bytes and preserved history. Source bytes may remain owned elsewhere.

## Control and compatibility

ControlledKernelResources requires every paint/clip/stroke method explicitly,
with WorkControl and Result. There is no default implementation, blanket legacy
adapter, fake paint, precharge substitute, Unsupported backend or smaller stop
limit. ControlledSampleInput passes the actual control into paint; lower typed
ControlledSampleKernel/ControlledIndexKernel/ControlledFlatKernel expose actual
job resources. New sample/index fixtures exercise these public interfaces.

The explicit TEST provider loops over stop data, charges PaintVisit at each real
iteration and propagates cancellation/work limit from inside the loop. It has
no production registration. The 4x4 fixture passes the same (s+0.5)/4 lattice,
stop slices and (sum+8)/16 rounding. This proves interface/data/control behavior,
not complete paint/stroke/render oracle parity. The full lower engines and root
coordinator providers remain separate scopes, as frozen in the order.

Legacy public structs/fields/required methods are unchanged. SceneView gains an
immutable source-owner accessor, implemented through a private borrowed Arc
witness; overlays/children preserve it, including empty allocations. No original
86 test file/assertion/literal was edited. All original 86 run alongside 25 new
checks. Protected hashes are recorded separately; full 603/157 source/oracle
acceptance, full app/runtime/performance/UI/live MCP/release are NOT claimed.

Final source-limit audit: shape_bounds.c defines 200M boundary marking WORK,
not bits. RasterJob::charge_boundary enforces that checked/cancelable per-mask counter
in its private live slot, so copied handles cannot fork/reset it; boundary
storage uses original engine-derived element bounds and the job budget, with no
new global byte default. The boundary-limit integration proof covers max/overflow/
cancellation and failed-charge identity.
use crate::{DASH_EPSILON, stopped};
use vexel_geometry::Edge;
use vexel_scene::{Result, SceneView, ShapeId, WorkControl, WorkKind};

pub fn dash_range_joins_seam(
    stroke: &vexel_scene::Stroke,
    dashes: &[f64],
    edges: &[Edge],
    first: usize,
    count: usize,
    control: &mut dyn WorkControl,
) -> Result<bool> {
    if dashes.is_empty()
        || dashes.len() > 16
        || count == 0
        || dashes.iter().any(|d| !d.is_finite() || *d <= 0.0)
    {
        return Ok(false);
    }
    let exp = dashes.len() * (if dashes.len() % 2 == 1 { 2 } else { 1 });
    let mut period = 0.0;
    for i in 0..exp {
        control.charge(WorkKind::StrokeTest, 1).map_err(stopped)?;
        period += dashes[i % dashes.len()]
    }
    if !period.is_finite() || period <= 0.0 {
        return Ok(false);
    }
    let mut phase = stroke.dash_offset % period;
    if !phase.is_finite() {
        return Ok(false);
    }
    if phase < 0.0 {
        phase += period
    }
    let mut pat = 0;
    while phase >= dashes[pat % dashes.len()] {
        phase -= dashes[pat % dashes.len()];
        pat = (pat + 1) % exp
    }
    let starts = pat % 2 == 0;
    let mut remain = dashes[pat % dashes.len()] - phase;
    if !remain.is_finite() || remain <= 0.0 {
        return Ok(false);
    }
    let mut ends = false;
    for i in 0..count {
        control.charge(WorkKind::StrokeTest, 1).map_err(stopped)?;
        let Some(e) = edges.get(first + i) else {
            return Ok(false);
        };
        let mut len = (e.b.x - e.a.x).hypot(e.b.y - e.a.y);
        while len > 0.0 {
            control.charge(WorkKind::StrokeTest, 1).map_err(stopped)?;
            let take = remain.min(len);
            ends = pat % 2 == 0;
            len -= take;
            remain -= take;
            if remain <= DASH_EPSILON {
                pat = (pat + 1) % exp;
                remain = dashes[pat % dashes.len()]
            }
        }
    }
    Ok(starts && ends)
}
pub fn subpath_closed_seam(
    view: SceneView<'_>,
    id: ShapeId,
    subpath: usize,
    edges: &[Edge],
    control: &mut dyn WorkControl,
) -> Result<bool> {
    let Some(shape) = view.shape(id) else {
        return Ok(false);
    };
    let Some(path) = shape
        .subpaths
        .slice(view.path_subpaths)
        .and_then(|v| v.get(subpath))
    else {
        return Ok(false);
    };
    let Some(dashes) = shape.stroke.dash_values.slice(view.dash_values) else {
        return Ok(false);
    };
    if !path.closed {
        return Ok(false);
    }
    dash_range_joins_seam(
        &shape.stroke,
        dashes,
        edges,
        path.first_edge,
        path.edge_count,
        control,
    )
}
pub fn shape_closed_seam(
    view: SceneView<'_>,
    id: ShapeId,
    edges: &[Edge],
    control: &mut dyn WorkControl,
) -> Result<bool> {
    let Some(shape) = view.shape(id) else {
        return Ok(false);
    };
    let Some(dashes) = shape.stroke.dash_values.slice(view.dash_values) else {
        return Ok(false);
    };
    if !shape
        .subpaths
        .slice(view.path_subpaths)
        .unwrap_or(&[])
        .is_empty()
    {
        for (i, subpath) in shape
            .subpaths
            .slice(view.path_subpaths)
            .unwrap()
            .iter()
            .enumerate()
        {
            control.charge(WorkKind::StrokeTest, 1).map_err(stopped)?;
            if subpath.closed && subpath_closed_seam(view, id, i, edges, control)? {
                return Ok(true);
            }
        }
        return Ok(false);
    }
    if !shape.stroke_closed {
        return Ok(false);
    }
    dash_range_joins_seam(
        &shape.stroke,
        dashes,
        edges,
        shape.edges.first,
        shape.edges.count,
        control,
    )
}
use crate::{DASH_CACHE_MAX_STEPS, STROKE_GRID_JOIN_BIT, stopped};
use vexel_geometry::{Edge, Point};
use vexel_scene::{
    DashJoin, DashSegment, JobDashCache, JobDashRange, JobRasterScratch, Linecap, RasterJob,
    RasterPool, Result, SceneView, Stroke, WorkControl, WorkKind,
};

fn dash_limit() -> vexel_scene::Diagnostic {
    vexel_scene::Diagnostic {
        kind: vexel_scene::ErrorKind::Limit(vexel_scene::LimitKind::DashCache),
        offset: 0,
    }
}
fn range(first: usize, end: usize) -> Result<vexel_scene::TableRange> {
    Ok(vexel_scene::TableRange {
        first,
        count: end.checked_sub(first).ok_or_else(dash_limit)?,
    })
}
struct Writer<'a> {
    job: &'a mut RasterJob,
    cache: JobDashCache,
    steps: usize,
}
impl Writer<'_> {
    fn ensure<T: vexel_scene::JobElement>(
        job: &mut RasterJob,
        handle: vexel_scene::JobBuffer<T>,
        needed: usize,
        control: &mut dyn WorkControl,
    ) -> Result<()> {
        let current = job.capacity(handle)?;
        if needed <= current {
            return Ok(());
        }
        let mut capacity = if current == 0 { 32 } else { current };
        while capacity < needed {
            capacity = capacity
                .checked_add((capacity / 8).max(1))
                .ok_or_else(dash_limit)?;
        }
        job.reserve(handle, capacity, control)
    }
    fn step(&mut self, n: usize, control: &mut dyn WorkControl) -> Result<()> {
        if n > DASH_CACHE_MAX_STEPS.saturating_sub(self.steps) {
            return Err(dash_limit());
        }
        control
            .charge(WorkKind::StrokeTest, n as u64)
            .map_err(stopped)?;
        self.steps += n;
        Ok(())
    }
    fn segment(
        &mut self,
        edge: Edge,
        start_cap: Linecap,
        end_cap: Linecap,
        control: &mut dyn WorkControl,
    ) -> Result<()> {
        let needed = self
            .job
            .slice(self.cache.segments)?
            .len()
            .checked_add(1)
            .ok_or_else(dash_limit)?;
        Self::ensure(self.job, self.cache.segments, needed, control)?;
        let segment = DashSegment {
            edge,
            start_cap,
            end_cap,
        };
        self.job.extend(self.cache.segments, &[segment], control)
    }
    fn join(&mut self, a: Edge, b: Edge, control: &mut dyn WorkControl) -> Result<()> {
        let needed = self
            .job
            .slice(self.cache.joins)?
            .len()
            .checked_add(1)
            .ok_or_else(dash_limit)?;
        Self::ensure(self.job, self.cache.joins, needed, control)?;
        self.job.extend(
            self.cache.joins,
            &[DashJoin {
                previous: a.a,
                vertex: a.b,
                next: b.b,
            }],
            control,
        )
    }
}
fn dashed(
    w: &mut Writer<'_>,
    stroke: &Stroke,
    dashes: &[f64],
    edges: &[Edge],
    first: usize,
    count: usize,
    closed: bool,
    implicit: bool,
    seam: bool,
    control: &mut dyn WorkControl,
) -> Result<()> {
    let mut n = count;
    if !closed && implicit && n > 0 {
        n -= 1;
    }
    if n == 0 {
        return Ok(());
    }
    if dashes.is_empty() || dashes.len() > 16 {
        return Err(dash_limit());
    }
    let exp = dashes
        .len()
        .checked_mul(if dashes.len() % 2 == 1 { 2 } else { 1 })
        .ok_or_else(dash_limit)?;
    w.step(exp, control)?;
    let mut period = 0.0;
    for i in 0..exp {
        let d = dashes[i % dashes.len()];
        if !d.is_finite() || d <= 0.0 || !(period + d).is_finite() {
            return Err(dash_limit());
        }
        period += d;
    }
    if period <= 0.0 {
        return Err(dash_limit());
    }
    let mut phase = stroke.dash_offset % period;
    if !phase.is_finite() {
        return Err(dash_limit());
    }
    if phase < 0.0 {
        phase += period;
    }
    let mut pat = 0usize;
    for _ in 0..=exp {
        if phase < dashes[pat % dashes.len()] {
            break;
        }
        w.step(1, control)?;
        phase -= dashes[pat % dashes.len()];
        pat = (pat + 1) % exp;
    }
    let mut remain = dashes[pat % dashes.len()] - phase;
    if !remain.is_finite() || remain <= 0.0 {
        return Err(dash_limit());
    }
    let mut joins_prev = false;
    for i in 0..n {
        w.step(1, control)?;
        let e = *edges
            .get(first.checked_add(i).ok_or_else(dash_limit)?)
            .ok_or_else(dash_limit)?;
        let dx = e.b.x - e.a.x;
        let dy = e.b.y - e.a.y;
        let len = dx.hypot(dy);
        if !len.is_finite() {
            return Err(dash_limit());
        }
        if len == 0.0 {
            continue;
        }
        let (mut at, mut cont) = (0.0, false);
        while at < len {
            w.step(1, control)?;
            let take = remain.min(len - at);
            let end = at + take;
            if take <= 0.0 || !end.is_finite() {
                return Err(dash_limit());
            }
            let on = pat % 2 == 0;
            let continues = on && end == len && remain - take > 1.0e-12;
            let cross = continues && i + 1 < n;
            if on {
                let a = Point {
                    x: e.a.x + dx * (at / len),
                    y: e.a.y + dy * (at / len),
                };
                let b = Point {
                    x: e.a.x + dx * (end / len),
                    y: e.a.y + dy * (end / len),
                };
                let sc = if at == 0.0 && (joins_prev || (seam && i == 0)) {
                    Linecap::Butt
                } else {
                    stroke.cap
                };
                let ec = if cross || (end == len && seam && i + 1 == n) {
                    Linecap::Butt
                } else {
                    stroke.cap
                };
                w.segment(Edge { a, b }, sc, ec, control)?;
            }
            if cross {
                cont = true;
            }
            at = end;
            remain -= take;
            if remain <= 1.0e-12 {
                pat = (pat + 1) % exp;
                remain = dashes[pat % dashes.len()];
            }
        }
        if cont && i + 1 < n {
            w.join(
                e,
                *edges.get(first + i + 1).ok_or_else(dash_limit)?,
                control,
            )?;
        }
        joins_prev = cont;
    }
    if seam {
        w.join(
            *edges.get(first + n - 1).ok_or_else(dash_limit)?,
            *edges.get(first).ok_or_else(dash_limit)?,
            control,
        )?;
    }
    Ok(())
}
fn solid(
    w: &mut Writer<'_>,
    stroke: &Stroke,
    edges: &[Edge],
    first: usize,
    count: usize,
    closed: bool,
    implicit: bool,
    control: &mut dyn WorkControl,
) -> Result<()> {
    let mut n = count;
    if !closed && implicit && n > 0 {
        n -= 1;
    }
    if n == 0 {
        return Ok(());
    }
    for i in 0..n {
        w.step(1, control)?;
        let e = *edges
            .get(first.checked_add(i).ok_or_else(dash_limit)?)
            .ok_or_else(dash_limit)?;
        let cap = if !closed && (i == 0 || i + 1 == n) {
            stroke.cap
        } else {
            Linecap::Butt
        };
        w.segment(e, cap, cap, control)?;
    }
    let joins = if closed { n } else { n - 1 };
    for i in 0..joins {
        w.step(1, control)?;
        let next = if closed { (i + 1) % n } else { i + 1 };
        w.join(

        w.join(
            edges[first + (next + n - 1) % n],
            edges[first + next],
            control,
        )?;
    }
    Ok(())
}

/// Build dash records directly in the admitted same-job buffers. The returned
/// descriptor has no borrowed source or temporary cache storage.
pub fn build_dash_cache(
    view: SceneView<'_>,
    local_edges: &[Edge],
    seams: &[bool],
    job: &mut RasterJob,
    scratch: &mut JobRasterScratch,
    control: &mut dyn WorkControl,
) -> Result<JobDashCache> {
    if view.shapes.len() > 65_536 {
        return Err(vexel_scene::Diagnostic {
            kind: vexel_scene::ErrorKind::Limit(vexel_scene::LimitKind::Shapes),
            offset: 0,
        });
    }
    job.validate_source(view.source_owner())?;
    // Build into new admitted buffers. The published cache remains intact until
    // dash records and every grid finish successfully; growth accounts for the
    // real old/new overlap through RasterJob's ChargeLedger admission.
    let segments = job.buffer(RasterPool::Dash, usize::MAX, control)?;
    let joins = match job.buffer(RasterPool::Dash, usize::MAX, control) {
        Ok(handle) => handle,
        Err(error) => {
            let _ = job.release(segments);
            return Err(error);
        }
    };
    let shapes = match job.buffer(RasterPool::Dash, 65_536, control) {
        Ok(handle) => handle,
        Err(error) => {
            let _ = job.release(segments);
            let _ = job.release(joins);
            return Err(error);
        }
    };
    let desc = JobDashCache {
        segments,
        joins,
        shapes,
        build_steps: 0,
    };
    if let Err(error) = job.reserve(desc.shapes, view.shapes.len(), control) {
        let _ = release_cache(job, desc);
        return Err(error);
    }
    let empty_cells = if view.shapes.is_empty() {
        None
    } else {
        match job.buffer::<vexel_scene::GridCell>(RasterPool::Grid, 0, control) {
            Ok(handle) => Some(handle),
            Err(error) => {
                let _ = release_cache(job, desc);
                return Err(error);
            }
        }
    };
    let empty_refs = if view.shapes.is_empty() {
        None
    } else {
        match job.buffer::<u32>(RasterPool::Grid, 0, control) {
            Ok(handle) => Some(handle),
            Err(error) => {
                if let Some(cells) = empty_cells {
                    let _ = job.release(cells);
                }
                let _ = release_cache(job, desc);
                return Err(error);
            }
        }
    };
    let result = (|| {
        let mut w = Writer {
            job,
            cache: desc,
            steps: 0,
        };
        for (i, shape) in view.shapes.iter().enumerate() {
            w.step(1, control)?;
            let segment_first = w.job.slice(desc.segments)?.len();
            let join_first = w.job.slice(desc.joins)?.len();
            if shape.stroke.rgba[3] != 0 && shape.stroke.width > 0.0 {
                let dashes = shape
                    .stroke
                    .dash_values
                    .slice(view.dash_values)
                    .ok_or_else(dash_limit)?;
                let subpaths = shape
                    .subpaths
                    .slice(view.path_subpaths)
                    .ok_or_else(dash_limit)?;
                if !subpaths.is_empty() {
                    for (si, sub) in subpaths.iter().enumerate() {
                        let seam = seams
                            .get(view.shapes.len() + shape.subpaths.first + si)
                            .copied()
                            .unwrap_or(false);
                        if dashes.is_empty() {
                            solid(
                                &mut w,
                                &shape.stroke,
                                local_edges,
                                sub.first_edge,
                                sub.edge_count,
                                sub.closed,
                                true,
                                control,
                            )?;
                        } else {
                            dashed(
                                &mut w,
                                &shape.stroke,
                                dashes,
                                local_edges,
                                sub.first_edge,
                                sub.edge_count,
                                sub.closed,
                                true,
                                seam,
                                control,
                            )?;
                        }
                    }
                } else {
                    let seam = seams.get(i).copied().unwrap_or(false);
                    if dashes.is_empty() {
                        solid(
                            &mut w,
                            &shape.stroke,
                            local_edges,
                            shape.edges.first,
                            shape.edges.count,
                            shape.stroke_closed,
                            shape.filled,
                            control,
                        )?;
                    } else {
                        dashed(
                            &mut w,
                            &shape.stroke,
                            dashes,
                            local_edges,
                            shape.edges.first,
                            shape.edges.count,
                            shape.stroke_closed,
                            shape.filled,
                            seam,
                            control,
                        )?;
                    }
                }
            }
            let segment_end = w.job.slice(desc.segments)?.len();
            let join_end = w.job.slice(desc.joins)?.len();
            let range = JobDashRange {
                segments: range(segment_first, segment_end)?,
                joins: range(join_first, join_end)?,
                grid_cells: empty_cells.ok_or_else(dash_limit)?,
                grid_refs: empty_refs.ok_or_else(dash_limit)?,
                grid_min_x: 0.0,
                grid_min_y: 0.0,
                grid_cell_size: 0.0,
                grid_columns: 0,
                grid_rows: 0,
            };
            w.job.extend(desc.shapes, &[range], control)?;
        }
        let cache = JobDashCache {
            build_steps: w.steps,
            ..desc
        };
        crate::job_grid::build_stroke_grid(view, w.job, cache, control)?;
        Ok(JobDashCache {
            build_steps: w.steps,
            ..desc
        })
    })();
    if let Err(error) = result {
        let _ = release_cache(job, desc);
        if let Some(handle) = empty_cells {
            let _ = job.release(handle);
        }
        if let Some(handle) = empty_refs {
            let _ = job.release(handle);
        }
        return Err(error);
    }
    let cache = result?;
    release_cache(job, scratch.dash)?;
    scratch.dash = cache;
    Ok(cache)
}

fn release_cache(job: &mut RasterJob, cache: JobDashCache) -> Result<()> {
    let mut empty = None;
    let count = job.slice(cache.shapes)?.len();
    for i in 0..count {
        let range = job.slice(cache.shapes)?[i];
        if range.grid_columns != 0 {
            job.release(range.grid_cells)?;
            job.release(range.grid_refs)?;
        } else if empty.is_none() {
            empty = Some((range.grid_cells, range.grid_refs));
        }
    }
    if let Some((cells, refs)) = empty {
        job.release(cells)?;
        job.release(refs)?;
    }
    job.release(cache.segments)?;
    job.release(cache.joins)?;
    job.release(cache.shapes)
}

pub(crate) fn tagged_index(reference: u32) -> (bool, usize) {
    (
        reference & STROKE_GRID_JOIN_BIT != 0,
        (reference & !STROKE_GRID_JOIN_BIT) as usize,
    )
}
use crate::{
    STROKE_GRID_JOIN_BIT, STROKE_GRID_MAX_AXIS, STROKE_GRID_MAX_CELLS, STROKE_GRID_MAX_REFS,
    stopped,
};
use vexel_geometry::Point;
use vexel_scene::{
    DashSegment, GridCell, JobDashCache, JobDashRange, RasterJob, RasterPool, Result, SceneView,
    WorkControl, WorkKind,
};

fn cap_error() -> vexel_scene::Diagnostic {
    vexel_scene::Diagnostic {
        kind: vexel_scene::ErrorKind::Limit(vexel_scene::LimitKind::DashCache),
        offset: 0,
    }
}
fn capacity_fallback(error: vexel_scene::Diagnostic) -> bool {
    matches!(
        error.kind,
        vexel_scene::ErrorKind::Limit(vexel_scene::LimitKind::DashCache)
            | vexel_scene::ErrorKind::Limit(vexel_scene::LimitKind::Grid)
    )
}
fn bounds_segment(s: &DashSegment, radius: f64) -> [f64; 4] {
    let margin = if s.start_cap == vexel_scene::Linecap::Square
        || s.end_cap == vexel_scene::Linecap::Square
    {
        radius * std::f64::consts::SQRT_2
    } else {
        radius
    };
    [
        s.edge.a.x.min(s.edge.b.x) - margin,
        s.edge.a.y.min(s.edge.b.y) - margin,
        s.edge.a.x.max(s.edge.b.x) + margin,
        s.edge.a.y.max(s.edge.b.y) + margin,
    ]
}
fn join_bounds(p: Point, radius: f64) -> [f64; 4] {
    [p.x - radius, p.y - radius, p.x + radius, p.y + radius]
}
fn axis(x: f64, range: &JobDashRange, horizontal: bool) -> Option<usize> {
    let (origin, size, count) = if horizontal {
        (range.grid_min_x, range.grid_cell_size, range.grid_columns)
    } else {
        (range.grid_min_y, range.grid_cell_size, range.grid_rows)
    };
    let mut value = (x - origin) / size;
    if !value.is_finite() || value < -1.0 || count == 0 {
        return None;
    }
    if value < 0.0 {
        value = 0.0;
    }
    let cell = value.floor().min(count as f64 - 1.0);
    (cell >= 0.0).then_some(cell as usize)
}
fn bbox(b: [f64; 4], r: &JobDashRange) -> Option<(usize, usize, usize, usize)> {
    Some((
        axis(b[0], r, true)?,
        axis(b[1], r, false)?,
        axis(b[2], r, true)?,
        axis(b[3], r, false)?,
    ))
}
/// Build every shape grid in admitted same-job buffers. Oversized cell/ref/byte
/// grids follow the frozen scalar fallback; cancellation and admission errors
/// propagate without publishing a partially filled range.
pub(crate) fn build_stroke_grid(
    view: SceneView<'_>,
    job: &mut RasterJob,
    cache: JobDashCache,
    control: &mut dyn WorkControl,
) -> Result<()> {
    if job.slice(cache.shapes)?.len() != view.shapes.len() {
        return Err(vexel_scene::Diagnostic {
            kind: vexel_scene::ErrorKind::InvalidArgument,
            offset: 0,
        });
    }
    let mut total_cells = 0usize;
    let mut total_refs = 0usize;
    for i in 0..view.shapes.len() {
        control.charge(WorkKind::StrokeTest, 1).map_err(stopped)?;
        let mut range = *job.slice(cache.shapes)?.get(i).ok_or_else(cap_error)?;
        range.grid_min_x = 0.0;
        range.grid_min_y = 0.0;
        range.grid_cell_size = 0.0;
        range.grid_columns = 0;
        range.grid_rows = 0;
        let primitive = range
            .segments
            .count
            .checked_add(range.joins.count)
            .ok_or_else(cap_error)?;
        if primitive == 0 {
            job.slice_mut(cache.shapes)?[i] = range;
            continue;
        }
        let shape = &view.shapes[i];
        let radius = shape.stroke.width * 0.5;
        let mut minx = f64::INFINITY;
        let mut miny = f64::INFINITY;
        let mut maxx = f64::NEG_INFINITY;
        let mut maxy = f64::NEG_INFINITY;
        let sr = range.segments.first..range.segments.end().ok_or_else(cap_error)?;
        let jr = range.joins.first..range.joins.end().ok_or_else(cap_error)?;
        if sr.end > job.slice(cache.segments)?.len() || jr.end > job.slice(cache.joins)?.len() {
            return Err(vexel_scene::Diagnostic {
                kind: vexel_scene::ErrorKind::InvalidArgument,
                offset: 0,
            });
        }
        for index in sr.clone() {
            control.charge(WorkKind::StrokeTest, 1).map_err(stopped)?;
            let seg = job.slice(cache.segments)?[index];
            let b = bounds_segment(&seg, radius);
            minx = minx.min(b[0]);
            miny = miny.min(b[1]);
            maxx = maxx.max(b[2]);
            maxy = maxy.max(b[3]);
        }
        let jradii = if shape.stroke.join == vexel_scene::Linejoin::Miter {
            radius * shape.stroke.miter_limit
        } else {
            radius
        };
        for index in jr.clone() {
            control.charge(WorkKind::StrokeTest, 1).map_err(stopped)?;
            let j = job.slice(cache.joins)?[index];
            let b = join_bounds(j.vertex, jradii);
            minx = minx.min(b[0]);
            miny = miny.min(b[1]);
            maxx = maxx.max(b[2]);
            maxy = maxy.max(b[3]);
        }
        let sx = maxx - minx;
        let sy = maxy - miny;
        if !sx.is_finite() || !sy.is_finite() {
            job.slice_mut(cache.shapes)?[i] = range;
            continue;
        }
        let size = 1.0f64.max(sx.max(sy) / STROKE_GRID_MAX_AXIS as f64);
        let cols = (sx / size).ceil().max(1.0);
        let rows = (sy / size).ceil().max(1.0);
        if cols > 128.0 || rows > 128.0 {
            job.slice_mut(cache.shapes)?[i] = range;
            continue;
        }
        range.grid_min_x = minx;
        range.grid_min_y = miny;
        range.grid_cell_size = size;
        range.grid_columns = cols as u16;
        range.grid_rows = rows as u16;
        let cell_count = (cols as usize)
            .checked_mul(rows as usize)
            .ok_or_else(cap_error)?;
        if total_cells
            .checked_add(cell_count)
            .is_none_or(|n| n > STROKE_GRID_MAX_CELLS)
        {
            range.grid_columns = 0;
            range.grid_rows = 0;
            job.slice_mut(cache.shapes)?[i] = range;
            continue;
        }
        let cells_handle =
            job.buffer::<GridCell>(RasterPool::Grid, STROKE_GRID_MAX_CELLS, control)?;
        let mut refs_handle = None;
        let built = (|| -> Result<Option<(vexel_scene::JobBuffer<u32>, usize)>> {
            if let Err(error) = job.reserve(cells_handle, cell_count, control) {
                if capacity_fallback(error) {
                    return Ok(None);
                }
                return Err(error);
            }
            let zero = GridCell { first: 0, count: 0 };
            for _ in 0..cell_count {
                job.extend(cells_handle, &[zero], control)?;
            }
            let mut count = 0usize;
            let mut fits = true;
            for p in 0..primitive {
                control.charge(WorkKind::StrokeTest, 1).map_err(stopped)?;
                let b = if p < range.segments.count {
                    let seg = job.slice(cache.segments)?[range.segments.first + p];
                    bounds_segment(&seg, radius)
                } else {
                    let join =
                        job.slice(cache.joins)?[range.joins.first + p - range.segments.count];
                    join_bounds(join.vertex, jradii)
                };
                if p < range.segments.count
                    && ![b[0], b[1], b[2], b[3]].into_iter().all(f64::is_finite)
                {
                    fits = false;
                    break;
                }
                let Some((x0, y0, x1, y1)) = bbox(b, &range) else {
                    fits = false;
                    break;
                };
                for cy in y0..=y1 {
                    for cx in x0..=x1 {
                        control.charge(WorkKind::StrokeTest, 1).map_err(stopped)?;
                        let index = cy * cols as usize + cx;
                        let next = job.slice(cells_handle)?[index]
                            .count
                            .checked_add(1)
                            .ok_or_else(cap_error)?;
                        job.slice_mut(cells_handle)?[index].count = next;
                        count = count.checked_add(1).ok_or_else(cap_error)?;
                    }
                }
            }
            if !fits
                || total_refs
                    .checked_add(count)
                    .is_none_or(|n| n > STROKE_GRID_MAX_REFS)
            {
                return Ok(None);
            }
            let refs = job.buffer::<u32>(RasterPool::Grid, STROKE_GRID_MAX_REFS, control)?;
            refs_handle = Some(refs);
            if let Err(error) = job.reserve(refs, count, control) {
                if capacity_fallback(error) {
                    return Ok(None);
                }
                return Err(error);
            }
            for _ in 0..count {
                job.extend(refs, &[0u32], control)?;
            }
            let mut offset = 0usize;
            for cell in job.slice_mut(cells_handle)? {
                let n = cell.count;
                cell.first = offset;
                cell.count = 0;
                offset = offset.checked_add(n).ok_or_else(cap_error)?;
            }
            for p in 0..primitive {
                control.charge(WorkKind::StrokeTest, 1).map_err(stopped)?;
                let b = if p < range.segments.count {
                    let seg = job.slice(cache.segments)?[range.segments.first + p];
                    bounds_segment(&seg, radius)
                } else {
                    let join =
                        job.slice(cache.joins)?[range.joins.first + p - range.segments.count];
                    join_bounds(join.vertex, jradii)
                };
                let (x0, y0, x1, y1) = bbox(b, &range).ok_or_else(cap_error)?;
                let encoded = if p < range.segments.count {
                    let index = range.segments.first + p;
                    if index >= STROKE_GRID_JOIN_BIT as usize {
                        return Err(cap_error());
                    }
                    u32::try_from(index).map_err(|_| cap_error())?
                } else {
                    let index = range.joins.first + p - range.segments.count;
                    if index >= STROKE_GRID_JOIN_BIT as usize {
                        return Err(cap_error());
                    }
                    STROKE_GRID_JOIN_BIT | index as u32
                };
                for cy in y0..=y1 {
                    for cx in x0..=x1 {
                        control.charge(WorkKind::StrokeTest, 1).map_err(stopped)?;
                        let cell_index = cy * cols as usize + cx;
                        let cell = job.slice(cells_handle)?[cell_index];
                        let ref_index = cell.first.checked_add(cell.count).ok_or_else(cap_error)?;
                        job.slice_mut(refs)?[ref_index] = encoded;
                        job.slice_mut(cells_handle)?[cell_index].count += 1;
                    }
                }
            }
            Ok(Some((refs, count)))
        })();
        match built {
            Ok(Some((refs, count))) => {
                range.grid_cells = cells_handle;
                range.grid_refs = refs;
                total_cells += cell_count;
                total_refs += count;
                job.slice_mut(cache.shapes)?[i] = range;
            }
            Ok(None) => {
                if let Some(refs) = refs_handle {
                    job.release(refs)?;
                }
                job.release(cells_handle)?;
                range.grid_columns = 0;
                range.grid_rows = 0;
                job.slice_mut(cache.shapes)?[i] = range;
            }
            Err(error) => {
                if let Some(refs) = refs_handle {
                    let _ = job.release(refs);
                }
                let _ = job.release(cells_handle);
                return Err(error);
            }
        }
    }
    Ok(())
}
use vexel_scene::{GridCell, JobDashRange, ValidatedDashView};

fn axis(value: f64, origin: f64, size: f64, count: u16) -> Option<usize> {
    let mut cell = (value - origin) / size;
    if !cell.is_finite() || cell < -1.0 || count == 0 {
        return None;
    }
    if cell < 0.0 {
        cell = 0.0;
    }
    let cell = cell.floor().min(count as f64 - 1.0);
    (cell >= 0.0).then_some(cell as usize)
}

pub(crate) fn job_grid_lookup<'a>(
    range: &JobDashRange,
    cells: &'a [GridCell],
    x: f64,
    y: f64,
) -> Option<&'a GridCell> {
    let col = axis(
        x,
        range.grid_min_x,
        range.grid_cell_size,
        range.grid_columns,
    )?;
    let row = axis(y, range.grid_min_y, range.grid_cell_size, range.grid_rows)?;
    cells.get(
        row.checked_mul(range.grid_columns as usize)?
            .checked_add(col)?,
    )
}

/// Look up a validated job-owned stroke-grid cell by shape and local point.
pub fn grid_lookup(cache: ValidatedDashView<'_>, shape: usize, x: f64, y: f64) -> Option<GridCell> {
    let (range, cells, _) = cache.grid_at(shape).ok()?;
    job_grid_lookup(range, cells, x, y).copied()
}

use crate::*;
